+# AgriSmart India v1 preparation
+
+Status: factual metadata and an original strict adapter prepared; no HTTP service or farmer feature enabled. Check [validation](../../../docs/upstream-integration/05-validation-and-changes.md) for actual checkpoint/runtime results.
+
+59 crops, 387 disease/condition classes, DINOv2 ViT-B/14, 224px. The model is an initial screening candidate, not laboratory diagnosis, severity measurement or an open-set plant detector. All current adapter results require review; confidence thresholds are unvalidated.
+
+Source and licence: [SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md](SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md), [MODEL_CARD.md](MODEL_CARD.md). The model authors state non-commercial research/education use; underlying dataset and redistribution restrictions need review. No upstream source code, translated advice, photos/audio or frontend/backend was copied. This adapter implements the documented inference mathematics independently.
+
+Download from project root:
+
+```powershell
+python ai/models/agrismart-india/scripts/download_weights.py
+python ai/models/agrismart-india/scripts/download_weights.py --verify-only
+python -m unittest discover -s ai/models/agrismart-india/tests -v
+```
+
+The exact pinned release goes into ignored `checkpoints/model.pt`. Partial files are never accepted; an existing invalid file is not overwritten. Keep model weights, personal images, Python environments and datasets outside version control. A receipt beside the checkpoint records hash/size but does not mark licence or prediction tests as passed.
+
+Future runtime, after dependency/licence review: create an isolated venv outside Git; resolve compatible CPU torch/torchvision/timm/Pillow from requirements, pin a tested lock, then run:
+
+```powershell
+python ai/models/agrismart-india/predict.py --image '..\SIH_2026-upstream-reference\samples\tomato_late_blight_1.jpg' --crop tomato --top 5
+```
+
+This command is not claimed to have succeeded in preparation. It requires a verified checkpoint plus ML packages. Model must be instantiated once per bounded worker, not per HTTP request. Missing/invalid checkpoint is a hard error, no mock/other-model fallback. The CLI only accepts a local path; the future private service accepts validated bytes, never arbitrary URLs.
+
+`crops.json` is a catalogue, not the head's index order; use checkpoint labels/crop_classes. Scores include both raw global and selected-crop conditional evidence. Preprocessing uses checkpoint mean/std, timm bicubic crop0.9, 224px and average original/mirror softmax. Orientation is normalized and EXIF dropped at our new input boundary; record this difference in parity evaluations.
+
+Image constraints: JPEG/PNG/WebP, <=8 MiB encoded, <=20 million pixels, single frame, minimum side 64px. Limits are proposed engineering safeguards, not agronomic quality validation. No leaf/OOD or calibrated uncertainty detector exists here. FastAPI contract: [CONTRACT.md](../../services/inference/CONTRACT.md).

