+++ b/ai/services/inference/CONTRACT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Private FastAPI inference contract v1
+
+Status: proposed, not an implemented FastAPI service. Reuse strict model adapter; do not copy upstream backend or add farmer CRUD here. `/backend` owns application security/orchestration/records.
+
+Network: private application service only, no public host port in production. Browser calls Next.js; backend calls FastAPI using server-only `Authorization: Bearer <AI_SERVICE_TOKEN>`. Constant-time credential validation, fail closed if missing; TLS at service boundary or equivalent protected transport. No farmer DB credentials, public CORS, arbitrary image URLs or runtime model download. Log only redacted request/model/latency/error metadata.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+| Method/path | Semantics |
+|---|---|
+| `GET /health` | Process liveness, minimal status; no checkpoint path/secrets |
+| `GET /ready` | 200 only when exact verified model loaded/warmed and worker available; otherwise 503. No mock success. Internal/probe access only |
+| `GET /v1/model/metadata` | Authenticated version/checkpoint/taxonomy/preprocess identity, crop keys/class labels, limitations |
+| `POST /v1/predict` | Authenticated multipart: `image` JPEG/PNG/WebP, optional exact supported `crop`, `top_k` integer 1..10 (default 5) |
+
+Suggested limits: encoded file <=8 MiB, body overhead bounded separately, <=20 MP, minimum side 64px, single frame, magic-byte/decoder validation, orientation correction/metadata removal; content-type alone is insufficient. Malformed/missing MIME should still be determined by decoded bytes. Blur/light checks may request a retake but cannot certify a plant. No HEIC decoder selected; report unsupported format with conversion/capture guidance.
+
+## Response
+
+```json
+{
+  "schemaVersion": "1",
+  "requestId": "opaque",
+  "mode": "real",
+  "selectedCrop": "tomato",
+  "model": {
+    "version": "india-model-v1",
+    "sha256": "ffaffb1e3ca0a81831454e8268b11cf2d16b418838042b023ad188f79e61a08a",
+    "taxonomyVersion": "checkpoint-sha-bound",
+    "preprocessing": "timm-bicubic-crop0.9-224-tta-mirror-v1"
+  },
+  "predictions": [
+    {"label": "tomato::Early blight", "rawScore": 0.30, "score": 0.60}
+  ],
+  "scoreType": "crop_conditioned_softmax",
+  "cropScores": {"tomato": 0.50},
+  "selectedCropMass": 0.50,
+  "uncertainty": {"status": "REVIEW_REQUIRED", "reasons": ["FIELD_POLICY_NOT_VALIDATED", "NO_OOD_DETECTOR"]},
+  "quality": {"status": "NOT_AGRONOMICALLY_VALIDATED", "warnings": []},
+  "isLaboratoryConfirmed": false,
+  "severity": null,
+  "processingMs": 0
+}
+```
+
+Illustrative numbers and truncated cropScores only; actual cropScores must represent the full global crop distribution. `processingMs=0` is a placeholder, never a claimed runtime. Model adapter returns inference fields; the future service adds schemaVersion/requestId/quality/timing/taxonomyVersion after validation. Return top-k alternatives, not a single confident label. Scores are model evidence, not calibrated disease probability. Invalid/unsupported photos yield no predictions; uncertain valid photos may return candidates with review/retake advice. Human review does not alter original model evidence.
+
+Error: `{"error":{"code":"CROP_UNSUPPORTED","message":"Selected crop is not supported.","requestId":"opaque"}}`. Statuses: 401 missing/wrong service credential; 400 malformed multipart; 413 encoded/pixel cap; 415 format; 422 decode/dimensions/crop/top_k; 429 bounded queue capacity; 503 unavailable/unverified model; 504 deadline; 500 generic internal error. Do not return raw exceptions. Frontend receives backend's normalized envelope, not this internal payload directly.
+
+Startup: validate configuration/manifest, verify size/SHA before safe torch deserialization, validate class order/metadata, instantiate model once, warm up and declare readiness. One bounded inference worker initially; queue capacity/timeouts/cancellation tested before production. Liveness remains distinct from readiness. Shutdown drains/cancels bounded work. Separate CPU PyTorch/timm/Pillow requirements from FastAPI/uvicorn/python-multipart; final service dependency lock is future work.

